# brain-db scope for the WEDNESDAY seat (Secuura + general).
# This file IS the allow-list: a path enters the index only if an `allow` line
# matches it. Each allow line is: allow <kind> <directory>/<file-name pattern>
# (one directory, no recursion, no symlinks; .md only, .tsv for the rules index).
# Paths are relative to the tree root. Lines starting with # are comments.

seat wednesday
own_clients secuura general wednesday wed
deny_clients datasec

# The seat's own rules files, one row per numbered rule or heading section. A file at
# the tree root is named exactly (no pattern).
allow rules        CLAUDE.md
allow rules        0_Brain/CLAUDE.md
allow lesson       0_Brain/learnings/20*.md
allow rules_index  0_Brain/learnings/_rules_index.tsv
allow ledger       0_Brain/learnings/_ledger.md
allow ledger       0_Brain/learnings/_ledger_archive.md
allow daily        0_Brain/daily/20*.md
allow skill        0_Brain/skills/*.md
allow identity     0_Brain/identity/*.md
allow people       0_Brain/people/*.md
allow architecture 1_Project_Definition/Architecture/*.md

# LESSONS are decided by content, not by name (Wednesday's ruling, ANSWER-1 item 2):
#   - excluded when the frontmatter tier names a deny_clients client (or is a
#     project tier naming none of own_clients);
#   - excluded when the lesson has rows in the rules index and EVERY row's seats
#     column names only other seats; a lesson with no row is decided by tier alone.

# Sync leftovers: excluded wherever the text appears in the tree-relative path.
deny_path (conflict_on_
deny_path .pre-

# Another seat's own RECORDS: the word excludes a path when it is in a FOLDER
# name (any kind: daily_tuesday/, 2_Project_Files/tuesday/), or in the FILE name
# of a record kind (ledger, daily). It never excludes a lesson, skill or
# architecture file by its name.
deny_seat_word tuesday
deny_seat_word friday
deny_seat_word laptop_datasec
